{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/28701-mummy-the-curse-gmc-updates","id":28701,"title":"Mummy: the Curse - GMC updates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-12T07:09:21-08:00","id":28701,"title":"Mummy: the Curse - GMC updates","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This is not of my making, but I thought that it was important to save this from the old forums. If JMobius wants to take charge of this again, I can delete this post. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Special Elite\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Mummy: the Curse - GMC Update</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><i><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Copied from the White-Wolf forums; most material by JMobius</span></i></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Character Creation and XP</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Starting mummies get 5 XP.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Acclimatized Arisen get 10 XP.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Descent Veterans get 20 XP.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Legendary Immortals get 30 XP. </span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\">Experience Costs</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Attributes - 3 XP</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Skills - 2 XP</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Skill Specialties - 1 XP</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Merits - 1 XP</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Willpower Dots - 1 XP</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Affinities - 5 XP</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Favored or Fated Affinities - 4 XP</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Utterances - 5 XP</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Defining Pillar - 1 XP</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Other Pillars - 2 XP</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Memory - 3 XP</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Affinities may be liquidated for 2 XP.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Mummy Properties</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Mummies now take bashing damage from all mundane non-flame sources.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Memory</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">TODO: Memory mechanics are probably alright as is. Sybarite XP needs looking at.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Merits</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Encyclopedic Knowledge costs one dot for mummies.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Language behaves as described in Mummy, but the GMC Merit Multilingual gives three languages, rather than two.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">? Should Guild Status include any additional bonuses, like some aspects of Professional Training.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">? Should Witness be lowered from three dots to two?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">TODO: Review Cult</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Sybaris</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">TODO: Could be better expressed using Conditions and the Aura rules demoed for Blood and Smoke.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Affinities</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Ancient Horror Unveiling</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Characters whose Virtue espouses the theme of Courage do not have their opposed roll\u2019s target number increased.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Instead of inflicting the Phobia derangement, the power inflicts the Witness to Horror Condition.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Instead of inflicting the Hysteria and Avoidance derangements, the power inflicts the Consumed by Horror condition.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Witness to Horror</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Effect: You have born witness to a mummy's terrible visage, and cannot bear close proximity, preferring to give her a wide berth. Any attacks made against your terrifying foe take a -5 penalty.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: Six weeks pass since being subjected to Ancient Horror Unveiling.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Beat: Should you become trapped by the mummy, unable to flee, you may gain a Beat by cowering in fear, taking no actions, until a chance for escape arises.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Consumed by Horror</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Effect: You have seen the monster's true face, and you cannot let it happen again. You are extremely hesitant to go anywhere that you know risks another encounter with the mummy, especially her tomb. Should the worst happen, and you are once again confronted by the mummy, you are driven to flee the scene as swiftly as possible. You are too overwhelmed by fear to make any attacks against the mummy while in her presence.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: Two weeks pass since being subjected to Ancient Horror Unveiling.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Beat: You gain a beat when your fearful and avoidant behavior meaningfully inconveniences you in some fashion, such as gaining the ire of your companions when you abandon your lookout post, for fear that the mummy might be nearby.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">? Dauntless Explorer substitutes Iron Stamina \u25cf for Strong Back in both locations.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">? Dominating Might is okay as is.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">? Enlightened Senses grants the one-dot version of Meditative Mind.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Glorious Mein grants the two-dot version of Striking Looks.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Nihilist Awakening revised:</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Nihilist Awakening</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Characters whose Virtue espouses a theme of commitment to something larger than themselves do not have their opposed roll\u2019s target number increased.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Instead of inflicting the Depression derangement, the power inflicts the Nihilist's Wisdom Condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Instead of inflicting the Melancholia derangement, the power inflicts the Tasting Futility condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Nihilist's Wisdom</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Effect: Your eyes have been opened, and you know that nothing you do will last. Once per scene, if you fail a roll that you actively apply yourself toward, you lose one Willpower and cannot spend any for the remainder of the scene.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: A month passes since being subjected to Nihilist Awakening.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Tasting Futility</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Effect: Whenever you suffer the effects of the Nihilist's Wisdom Condition, you also suffer an additional -2 to all rolls for the remainder of the scene.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: A week passes since being subjected to Nihilist's Awakening.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Paragon Shames the Weak</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Instead of inflicting the Inferiority Complex derangement, the power inflicts the Moment of Doubt Condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Instead of inflicting the Melancholia derangement, the power inflicts the Too Small To Succeed Condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Instead of inflicting the Irrationality derangement, the power inflicts the It Isn't My Fault! Condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Moment of Doubt</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Effect: Your confidence has been broken, and doubt in your abilities continually nags at your mind. If you ever are forced into a situation where a single roll is pivotal, you suffer -1 to all rolls for the remainder of the scene (including the triggering roll).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: A month passes since being subjected to Paragon Shames the Weak.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Too Small to Succeed</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Effect: When the weight falls upon your shoulders, you are certain you will crumble beneath it. Whenever you suffer the effects of the Moment of Doubt Condition, you also suffer an additional -1 to all rolls for the remainder of the scene. In addition, you cannot spend Willpower for the remainder of the scene.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: A week passes since being subjected to Paragon Shames the Weak.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">It Isn't My Fault!</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Effect: You cannot bear the burden of your own weakness. Whenever you fail, or are accused of failure, you must </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\">verbally </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">lash out at all those involved. You must stop short of starting violence, but your comments may well cause the other party to initiate.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: A day passes since being subjected to Paragon Shames the Weak.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Beat: You provocations result in harm for you, be it physically, or through loss of friends, contacts, or resources.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Radiant Lifeforce grants the following Condition, instead of the Quick Healer merit:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Touched By Sekhem</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">All of your natural healing rates are doubled.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Special: With sleep or successful meditation while under this condition, you may grasp hold of the lifeforce welling within you, and be transformed. You may spend a Willpower dot to make this Condition persistent.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: If this condition is not Persistent, it ends when you exit the area of effect of all mummies with the Font of Radiance affinity.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Voice of Conscience inflicts the following Condition:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Nagging Conscience</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The next time you encounter an opportunity to exercise the targeted Virtue, you must do so, unless doing so would clearly be suicidal.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: You satisfy the specified Virtue.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Voice of Temptation inflicts the following Condition:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Hungry Vice</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The next time you encounter an opportunity to exercise the targeted Vice, you must do so, unless doing so would clearly be suicidal.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: You satisfy the specified Vice.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Words Summoned Forth</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Characters whose Virtue espouses themes of humility or temperance do not have their opposed roll\u2019s target number increased.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Instead of inflicting the Vocalization derangement, the power inflicts the To Good Not To Share Condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Instead of inflicting the Narcissism derangement, the power inflicts the Just Call Me VIP Condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Instead of inflicting the Megalomania derangement, the power inflicts the I'll Show You All! Condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Too Good Not To Share</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Effect: You are prone to becoming so absorbed in your thoughts that you unknowingly speak them aloud.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: Three weeks pass since being subjected to Words Summoned Forth.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Beat: You gain a beat when your character unwittingly speaks sensitive information aloud in the presence of a hostile target.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Just Call Me VIP</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Effect: Your ego has been inflated to enormous sizes, and you have difficulty dealing with those who can't see it. You now suffer a -3 to teamwork rolls when you are not the primary actor, and suffer a -1 to all Socialize skill rolls.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: Two weeks pass since being subjected to Words Summoned Forth.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">I'll Show You All!</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Effect: Your vanity is unparalled. The teamwork penalty for Just Call Me VIP increases to -4, and the Socialize penalty to -2. If you ever fail a contested roll against someone you feel is your inferior, lose a point of Willpower as you try to struggle to contain your doubt and self-loathing.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Resolution: A week passes since being subjected to Words Summoned Forth.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Utterances</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Blessed is the God King, Tier 3: Replace the Fluid Attack merit reference with Flurry, the four-dot merit from the Light Weapons Fighting Style.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Cthonic Dominion, Tier 1: Rather than granting the Ghost Speech Numen, ghosts in the area of effect simply gain the ability to speak and be heard in the material world.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Cthonic Dominion, Tiers 2 &amp; 3: Subtract the ghost's Rank from the roll, rather than Resistance, Resolve, or Composure.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Command the Beasts, Tier 3: Rather than the Prudence Virtue, immunity should be extended to all Virtues which espouse a theme of rationality or calm.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">TODO: Some remaining Utterances need to be reviewed.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Doom Affliction, all tiers, might be better expressed as Conditions.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Dreams of Dead Gods, all tiers, inflict all manner of status effects and derangements. Needs a ton of Condition work here.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Dust Beneath Feet, Tier 2, references many combat mechanics.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Gift of the Golden Ankh, Tier 1, references Pride, and might inflict Conditions.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Gift of the Golden Ankh, Tier 2, references Envy, and a ton of merits.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Kiss of Apep, Tier 1, should inflict one hell of a nasty Condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Kiss of Apep, Tier 3, references Virtues and Derangements.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Power or Re, Tier 2, references Fire rules?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Power of Re, Tier 3, inflicts damage and references the Striking Looks merit.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Revelations of Smoke and Flame, Tier 1, inflicts damage.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Revelations of Smoke and Flame, Tier 2, references the Striking Looks merit.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Revelations of Smoke and Flame, Tier 3, references Justice and Wrath.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Rite of the Sacred Scarab, Tier 1, references combat mechanics.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Rite of the Sacred Scarab, Tier 3, needs all kinds of refactoring.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Secrets Ripped From Skies, Tiers 2 and 3 both inflict damage.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Seeds of Life, Tiers 2 and 3 might be represented as very interesting Conditions.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Torn Veil of Forgetting, Tier 3, can be a Memory sin.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Words of the Amanuensis, Tier 3, references the Language merit.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Words of Dead Speech, Words of Dead Hunger, and Words of Dead Fury reference a lot of Ghost rules.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Wrathful Desert Power, all tiers, inflict damage and interact with combat systems.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T07:41:43-08:00","id":50677,"title":"","content":"Looking at what JMobius put for costs with Affinities, I'm not sure. I don't think they're powerful enough to warrant 4-5XP as a cost. I would make it 2-3 (depending on if it's favored) to bring it more in line with Embeds/Exploits as Demons do them cost-wise, and maybe reduce Utterances to 4 xp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T09:24:23-08:00","id":50750,"title":"","content":"Utterances shouldn't be any higher than the highest affinity cost, as that's basically how they're handled in the pre-gmc. I think the XP costs in the other GMC thread kicking around this forum were right on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T11:26:18-08:00","id":50873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/28701-mummy-the-curse-gmc-updates?p=50677#post50677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at what JMobius put for costs with Affinities, I'm not sure. I don't think they're powerful enough to warrant 4-5XP as a cost. I would make it 2-3 (depending on if it's favored) to bring it more in line with Embeds/Exploits as Demons do them cost-wise, and maybe reduce Utterances to 4 xp.</div> </div> </div> </div>For costs, I'm using:<br /> <br /> Memory: 2<br /> Defining Pillar: 1<br /> Other Pillar: 2<br /> Favored Affinity: 3<br /> Other Affinity: 4<br /> Fated Affinity: As above, take a Beat<br /> Utterance: 3<br /> Willpower dot: 1<br /> <br /> I'm also awarding Sebayt Beats instead of Sebayt XP, under similar circumstances, with one exception. Achieving a new minimum Pillar level awards a Sebayt XP directly.<br /> <br /> I'm allowing Mummies to deliberately &quot;unleash&quot; their Sybaris. They roll Sekhem + (Favored Attribute), the first listed for Terror, the second for Unease, lasting for turns per success.<br /> <br /> I'm planning on madly winging it for anything involving Virtues and Vices, or anything that looks like it should be a Condition or Tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T02:26:13-08:00","id":52237,"title":"","content":"I think it would be cool to see the Mummy Lifeweb mechanics (as amorphous as they are) used as some sort of version of vampiric Touchstones, in a Memory related sense. Objects, and cultists, who the mummy NEEDS in its Lifeweb to keep its memory stable, and thus the Mummy itself also anchors the Lifeweb. Important relics, vestiges, rituals, cultists, ideals.. they could all be used to give the lifeweb a lot more depth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T06:46:21-08:00","id":52337,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, that would make the Lifeweb actually matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}